### Hardest finding (C)
**As stated, the design does not bind.** Handedness (§2) only gives two *distinct* channels, not an attractive one. \(\sum\theta_i=0\) only yields an \(O(1/N)\) mean-field effect that vanishes on a large fabric. Binding is a §7 *requirement*, not a *consequence*. Literal “partial cycle delivers nothing” also *suppresses* the usual exchange routes to forces, so static \(\xi\)-energy would have to do all the work — and no such energy is written down.

### Coherence (A)
| Claim | Verdict |
|-------|---------|
| Energy only in complete cycles | **Does not follow** from link mediation alone — needs a latch/monodromy/quantisation rule |
| \(c\) emerges | Speed *limit* \(\sim a/\tau\) **follows**; isotropic Lorentzian \(c\) does **not**; cycle rate stays an input |
| Mass = cell count | **Inconsistent** with exterior distortion if \(\xi\) carries mass — distortion mass is unlocated |
| 3-from-7 | **Unsupported** and **not load-bearing**; §2 only needs a 2D transverse plane |

### Particles (B)
All of §7 is undemonstrated. Multi-cell trapping is a *definition*, not an existence theorem. Discrete species and mass ratios are hopes. Only a speed *limit* of order \(a/\tau\) is a partial consequence.

### Implementation (D)
Not run. The design underdetermines the EOM; any simulator would add postulates. A full buildable spec with OPEN items is in §D of the review.

### Falsification (E)
Cheapest true kill: full 3D nonlinear pair survey of \(\Delta E(r)\) in both handedness channels after multi-cell objects exist. All channels non-attractive (or gate only restorable with a new field) kills the design on its own terms.
